@title SPUN
@author D. Rimron-Soutter
@-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@node MAIN
@next MENU
@{r}SPUN
@{c}@{h1}SPUN

SPUN is a package manager for the ZX Spectrum Next. It finds apps in the SPUN
catalogue, installs them on your Next, and updates the apps it installed.

SPUN is the dot command @{b}.spun@{ub}. It must be in @{i}C:/dot@{ui} with the name
@{i}spun@{ui}, so that it runs from any directory.

 @{" The SPUN menu " LINK MENU}
 @{" The .spun command " LINK COMMAND}
@-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@node MENU
@prev MAIN
@next COMMAND
@toc MAIN
@{r}SPUN
@{c}@{h1}The SPUN menu

Run @{b}spun.bas@{ub} to open the SPUN menu. When it starts, it moves
@{i}spun.dot@{ui} from its own directory to @{i}C:/dot/spun@{ui}, if the file is
there.

@{b}Browse the catalogue@{ub}
    Opens the SPUN browser, where you can find and install apps.

@{b}Update installed apps@{ub}
    Installs the latest release of each app that SPUN installed.

@{b}Install an app@{ub}
    Asks for the id or alias of an app, then installs it.

@{b}Read the guide@{ub}
    Opens this guide.

Use the cursor keys and @{b}ENTER@{ub} to choose. @{b}BREAK@{ub} closes the menu.
@-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@node COMMAND
@prev MENU
@toc MAIN
@{r}SPUN
@{c}@{h1}The .spun command

@{b}.spun [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]@{ub}

With no command, .spun opens the SPUN browser.

@{h2}Commands

@{b}find TEXT [PAGE]@{ub}
    Lists the apps that match TEXT. Put TEXT with spaces in quotes:
    .spun find "two words" 2

@{b}info APPID [PAGE]@{ub}
    Shows an app's details.

@{b}get APPID@{ub}
    Installs an app, then changes to the directory it is in. APPID can
    also be the app's alias.

@{b}update@{ub}
    Installs the latest release of each app that SPUN installed.

@{h2}Options

@{b}-s xxxx@{ub}    Use another server
@{b}-p xxxx@{ub}    Use another port
@{b}-q@{ub}         Quiet: print no progress lines, and show no splash screen
            when the browser opens
